The discrete domain, translation convention, flow presentations, and allowed quotients are not defined in the supplied question.

Source-record limitation: The two flow presentations, domain, and proposed quotient operations are not defined by the supplied extraction. The primary Oberwolfach Report 2025/12, p.\ 532, describes two flow presentations of alcoved polytopes using support numbers and facet volumes. The supplied reconstructed question instead names $L$-convex sets and functions. This is a disagreement about the mathematical objects, not merely missing definitions; no equivalence or corrected target is inferred, and the supplied statement is preserved.
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Describe the correspondence between the two flow-based presentations of $L$-convex sets and functions. Define natural quotient operations for $L$-convex sets and $L$-convex functions, and establish their basic structural properties. \href{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2025/12}{[S2]}
\paragraph{Source status.}
